hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-8 = unlines (cons "Receiving whole, which the knowledge transmission arc asks of its reader, is what a symbol was built for. A Greek *symbolon* was a token broken in two. Each party kept a half, and identity was proven when the halves fitted back together: *syn* + *ballein*, thrown together. A symbol is a proof of identity by fit. That is content addressing and it is the active pair: two halves meet, and if they fit, they are the same transaction. The opposite word is *diabolos*, *dia* + *ballein*, thrown across, thrown apart: the slanderer, the one who splits what belongs together. A symbolic nervous system is, in the words, a body of cords whose parts prove their identity by fitting together." nil)
